[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Native model admission and typed terminal adapter qualification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MODEL-NATIVE-ADMISSION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Validate each bulk-model parameter before native evaluation
STATEMENT: >>>
Bulk BSIM3 model admission shall independently reject a nonfinite numeric
parameter, invalid polarity, nonpositive oxide/doping/channel geometry, and
negative parasitic geometry. Zero parasitic geometry and a finite signed
threshold shall remain admissible, without implying device accuracy.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: bsim330_admission_checks_each_parameter_before_provider_calls
uses direct Rust objects and independently changed fields. Native bulk trials
are separately exercised by explicitly including the two ignored provider tests.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MODEL-NATIVE-PORT-VIEW-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve native model kind and D/G/S/body port order
STATEMENT: >>>
The element adapter shall preserve the four distinct D/G/S/body indices and
bulk-versus-FD-reference model kind. Non-native elements shall have no native
model view. FD-reference adapter evidence shall not imply FD-provider behavior.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: bsim330_native_accessor_preserves_four_terminal_order_and_kind
uses four distinct indices and both native element variants; no provider calls.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MODEL-PROVIDER-MUTATION-LANE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bind provider-dependent mutations to executed native tests
STATEMENT: >>>
Provider-dependent mutation evidence shall retain the tested source, exact
candidate names, trusted native asset hashes and explicitly enabled test scope.
Unavailable providers and excluded model families shall remain separate from
caught candidates and reviewed numerical equivalents.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Qualification lane:35bulk-model candidates and3adapter candidates, with trusted
Windows bulk host/model. SOI-domain guards have a separate validation-only lane;
missing FD-provider results shall not be presented as physical model evidence.
Results require reviewed native outcomes; start alone is not success.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MODEL-SOI-BIAS-DOMAIN-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Separate invalid SOI bias from provider availability
STATEMENT: >>>
The static FD-reference bias domain shall independently require each of its
four terminal voltages to be finite and within the inclusive interval [-6,6]V.
Out-of-domain input shall return InvalidInput before provider lookup. Valid
domain input may proceed to a provider result or a structured Unsupported
availability result; missing output shall not be replaced with zero.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: soi_bias_domain_preserves_independent_components_and_inclusive_edges
and soi_bias_domain_accepts_seeded_finite_interior_points,64Proptest cases,
seed2026111919. This is input/error-stage evidence, not FD-provider execution,
numerical-current accuracy or SOI dynamic-charge qualification.
Unsupported can represent any mapped host error. The qualification process
explicitly leaves the FD host unset; the assertions establish domain admission,
not a diagnosis of arbitrary host failures or proof of a usable model result.
<<<
